  "id": "frequency-selectivity",
  "term": "frequency selectivity",
  "definition": "Frequency selectivity is the auditory system’s ability to respond differently to sounds of different frequencies. In this source, it is reflected in how narrowly a neuron is tuned to particular frequencies, with narrower bandwidth indicating greater selectivity.",
